{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"abbb537a9a36237405cc1568909ad0f8c63473a8da57f7d5e3618503aa194d81","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar terraform infra / shared AWS resource adoption","key_entities":["snap-demo-tfstate-896586841071","rebar-tfstate-896586841071","token.actions.githubusercontent.com","arn:aws:iam::896586841071:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com","*.solutions.navateam.com","auth_host","rebar-terraform-plan","infra/terraform/iam.tf","infra/terraform","shared/terraform.tfstate","project=snap-demo","Project=rebar","ADR 0048","terraform-drift"],"problem_keywords":["terraform state ownership","resource re-homing","oidc provider","wildcard acm cert","sso stack","drift ci","import/apply/retag","shared aws account","state migration","tag ownership"],"propositions":["18 shared AWS resources owned by decommissioned snap must be re-homed into rebar's terraform and state.","rebar's rebar-terraform-plan drift role depends on the GitHub OIDC provider that snap's dead state currently owns, risking breakage if that state is destroyed.","The wildcard ACM cert and auth_host domain-wide SSO stack are orphaned in snap's dead state and must survive by moving ownership to rebar.","Adoption must preserve physical resource names to avoid destroy/recreate, changing only ownership and the project tag from project=snap-demo to Project=rebar.","Resources must be imported into rebar-tfstate, applied with no destroy/replace or secret rotation, and released from snap's shared/terraform.tfstate.","terraform-drift CI on main must be green with committed HCL matching live state after adoption."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785204680866992957,"uuid":"30dae2a0-708c-4599-8922-a4b29ced578a"}